{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_39d397a37459b4d4c13ec7435c234880113f5df3066204af384673b4d63bec1c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation describes IDE integrations: a VSCode extension (source in VSIX/, published as mufasa.snow-cli) and a JetBrains plugin (source in Jetbrains/), with configurable terminal, bell, git-blame, inline-completion, and next-edit settings."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4d3a07c029465e382278cad08c0bc65ad747cf9053a2336ef9192f4570abfd6b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"After installation the product is launched with the `snow` command, and installation can be verified with `snow --version` and `snow --help`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a2ae32f2e35c2fb58f64d7fb3ed86804deacf3c40e56bc5525b5c573c0f707b9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The documented runtime prerequisites are Node.js >= 18.x (ES2020 feature support) and npm >= 8.3.0."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f0f20bfcda544932e59786454330b851154384fbef08913dffaf659ace9a5487"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: building from source is done by cloning the repo, running npm install, then npm run link to build and globally link the snow command (npm run unlink to remove)."}],"claim_ids":["clm_39d397a37459b4d4c13ec7435c234880113f5df3066204af384673b4d63bec1c","clm_4d3a07c029465e382278cad08c0bc65ad747cf9053a2336ef9192f4570abfd6b","clm_a2ae32f2e35c2fb58f64d7fb3ed86804deacf3c40e56bc5525b5c573c0f707b9","clm_f0f20bfcda544932e59786454330b851154384fbef08913dffaf659ace9a5487"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:17:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_65425d40c4d840e9ba8c060ac0825371","id":"pg_daafa388ad3d547191a43de74c4d5abd","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/mayday-wpf-snow-cli-docs-usage-en-01-installation-guide-md-063b72c5c05-3de74c4d5abd.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_82b725e725345bb686b00b1e501ac590"],"title":"MayDay-wpf/snow-cli/docs/usage/en/01.Installation Guide.md @ 063b72c5c055","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:17:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_65425d40c4d840e9ba8c060ac0825371"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_35cfba37f73622135ae6e7fde0ede9d7dade02f39838d8b69a1a3c309a9a1f10"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Running snow creates a `~/.snow/` directory holding logs, configuration profiles, session history, async tasks, hooks, config.json for API settings, and settings.json including mcpServers."},{"claim_ids":["clm_39d397a37459b4d4c13ec7435c234880113f5df3066204af384673b4d63bec1c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation describes IDE integrations: a VSCode extension (source in VSIX/, published as mufasa.snow-cli) and a JetBrains plugin (source in Jetbrains/), with configurable terminal, bell, git-blame, inline-completion, and next-edit settings."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4d3a07c029465e382278cad08c0bc65ad747cf9053a2336ef9192f4570abfd6b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"After installation the product is launched with the `snow` command, and installation can be verified with `snow --version` and `snow --help`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6c8de81be64769c55bfa4963963099cc815faad911097084d75a67b86e4353da"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented operating modes include headless mode for command-line conversations and script integration, command injection in messages with security mechanisms, a vulnerability hunting mode, and an SSE service mode exposing API endpoints."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9fab0fdea8402b7da855ddec0821340bcd7264964f11bd86085e3314dff9a79a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A recommended ROLE.md defines the assistant's behavior: plan every step using a Plan Agent, maintain a TODO list via todo-manage (get/add/update/delete), locate files before reading, and record risks with notebook-add."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a2ae32f2e35c2fb58f64d7fb3ed86804deacf3c40e56bc5525b5c573c0f707b9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The documented runtime prerequisites are Node.js >= 18.x (ES2020 feature support) and npm >= 8.3.0."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b1206245df85850980fdc35cbe6f81934221c459a27379794ceb3819f660a43f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The documented source layout includes agents, LLM API adapters, React hooks for conversation, i18n, MCP, prompt templates, TypeScript types, Ink-based UI components, and utilities under source/."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b39d06b41c7f4444d55910eb85e08566674ef242066dfb1499be60248b7e2818"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Snow CLI is described as an agentic coding tool that runs in the terminal, distributed as the npm package snow-ai."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c8b6a1fce49c37e55ef7ff1a58253e86fe4e93592e6c252887024b28f9d2f424"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Feature docs cover sub-agent management and custom agents (including project Markdown agents), hooks for workflow automation, async background task management with sensitive-command approval, and a Team mode for multi-agent collaboration."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f0f20bfcda544932e59786454330b851154384fbef08913dffaf659ace9a5487"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: building from source is done by cloning the repo, running npm install, then npm run link to build and globally link the snow command (npm run unlink to remove)."}],"claim_ids":["clm_35cfba37f73622135ae6e7fde0ede9d7dade02f39838d8b69a1a3c309a9a1f10","clm_39d397a37459b4d4c13ec7435c234880113f5df3066204af384673b4d63bec1c","clm_4d3a07c029465e382278cad08c0bc65ad747cf9053a2336ef9192f4570abfd6b","clm_6c8de81be64769c55bfa4963963099cc815faad911097084d75a67b86e4353da","clm_9fab0fdea8402b7da855ddec0821340bcd7264964f11bd86085e3314dff9a79a","clm_a2ae32f2e35c2fb58f64d7fb3ed86804deacf3c40e56bc5525b5c573c0f707b9","clm_b1206245df85850980fdc35cbe6f81934221c459a27379794ceb3819f660a43f","clm_b39d06b41c7f4444d55910eb85e08566674ef242066dfb1499be60248b7e2818","clm_c8b6a1fce49c37e55ef7ff1a58253e86fe4e93592e6c252887024b28f9d2f424","clm_f0f20bfcda544932e59786454330b851154384fbef08913dffaf659ace9a5487"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:17:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_65425d40c4d840e9ba8c060ac0825371","id":"pg_eb568d7add7250c09f8404d2b546dd82","maturity":"dr